'<h4>7.7 Momento principal Mmin (tonf.m/m)</h4>
$Map{Mmin_sp(x; y) @ x = 0 : a & y = 0 : b}
#val
'<svg width="'svg_w'" height="'svg_h'" style="position:relative;margin-top:-'svg_h + 20'px;" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
#hide
#for jj = 0 : n_m
	#for ii = 0 : n_m
		cx_s = pad_l + ii*cw
		cy_s = pad_b + (n_m - jj)*ch
		val_s = Mmin_n.(ii + 1; jj + 1)
		#show
		#val
		'<circle cx="'cx_s'" cy="'cy_s'" r="6" fill="transparent" stroke="none"><title>Mmin('ii*d_x'; 'jj*d_y') = 'val_s' tonf.m/m</title></circle>
		#hide
	#loop
#loop
#show
#val
'</svg>
#equ
'<hr/>
'<h3>PARTE VII-b — Cortante transversal V13/V23 (corte de placa)</h3>
'<p>ETABS reporta V13/V23 incluso en ShellThin (Kirchhoff): aunque el elemento no tiene rigidez de corte, SAPFire lo recupera por equilibrio del campo de momentos (rutina ShellElem_RecoveryThickOnlySBR). Relacion ETABS: V = &tau;&middot;t.</p>
'<h4>7b.1 V13 (tonf/m) — V13 en ETABS</h4>
$Map{V13_sp(x; y) @ x = 0 : a & y = 0 : b}
'<h4>7b.2 V23 (tonf/m) — V23 en ETABS</h4>
$Map{V23_sp(x; y) @ x = 0 : a & y = 0 : b}
'<h4>7b.3 Vmax = &radic;(V13&sup2;+V23&sup2;) (tonf/m)</h4>
$Map{Vmax_sp(x; y) @ x = 0 : a & y = 0 : b}
'<hr/>
'<h3>PARTE VII-c — Comparacion losa Hekatan-DKE vs ETABS ShellThin (caso Live)</h3>
#hide
maxMxy = 0
maxw = 0
#for jj = 1 : n_m + 1
	#for ii = 1 : n_m + 1
		#if abs(Mxy_n.(ii; jj)) > maxMxy
			maxMxy = abs(Mxy_n.(ii; jj))
		#end if
		#if abs(w_field.(ii; jj)) > maxw
			maxw = abs(w_field.(ii; jj))
		#end if
	#loop
#loop
#show
#val
'<table border="1" cellpadding="6" style="border-collapse:collapse; font-size:0.95em">
'<tr style="background:#333;color:white"><th>Cantidad</th><th>Hekatan-DKE</th><th>ETABS ShellThin</th><th>Dif %</th></tr>
'<tr><td>max |Mxy| (tonf.m/m)</td><td>'maxMxy'</td><td>0.189</td><td>'(maxMxy/0.189 - 1)*100'</td></tr>
'<tr><td>max |V13| equilibrio (tonf/m)</td><td>'maxV13'</td><td>0.793</td><td>apoyo puntual (ver nota)</td></tr>
'<tr><td>max |V23| equilibrio (tonf/m)</td><td>'maxV23'</td><td>0.793</td><td>apoyo puntual (ver nota)</td></tr>
'<tr><td>max |w| (mm)</td><td>'maxw'</td><td>6.50</td><td>'(maxw/6.50 - 1)*100'</td></tr>
'</table>
#equ
'<p><b>MOMENTOS — resuelto (extraido de CsiGo2.dll + CSV ETABS):</b> el recovery de Mx/My/Mxy es IDENTICO al de ETABS: 2&times;2 Gauss en &xi;,&eta;=&plusmn;1/&radic;3 (=0.5773502691896257, 338&times; en el binario) + extrapolacion a nodos con factor &radic;3 (=1.7320508075688772, 47&times;), e integracion M=&sigma;<sub>flex</sub>&middot;t&sup2;/6 (verificado celda a celda contra el CSV de Mesa torsionT, caso Live). El residuo en Mxy (-4%) y w (-1.2%) NO es del recovery sino de la RIGIDEZ del elemento (DKE Batoz vs ShellThin de CSI).</p>
'<p><b>CORTE — formula CONFIRMADA:</b> V13 = &minus;(&part;M11/&part;x + &part;M12/&part;y), V23 = &minus;(&part;M22/&part;y + &part;M12/&part;x). Probado contra el CSV de ETABS (gradiente por-elemento de SUS momentos vs SU V13): <b>correlacion &minus;1.0000, max = 0.793 EXACTO</b> en los 25 elementos (script test_corte.py). El signo &minus; es convencion ETABS.</p>
'<p><b>Por que el V13 sale alto:</b> la FORMULA esta verificada EXACTA (test_corte.py: corr -1.000 vs ETABS). El exceso es MODELADO: las 4 columnas estan en las ESQUINAS como APOYO PUNTUAL &rarr; singularidad de cortante (V~1/r) que da gradientes de momento ~10&times; los de ETABS, el cual reparte la reaccion sobre la huella 0.4&times;0.4 (panel zone) &rarr; acota V13 a 0.793. Mxy (momento, finito) SI coincide. Para igualar V13 hay que modelar el footprint de columna. Ver doc maestro: validacion/MESA_TORSION_FUENTE_UNICA.md</p>
'<hr/>
'<h3>PARTE VIII — Diagramas viga Sur (B1, y=0)</h3>
'<p>5 segmentos de dx='d_x' m. Viga flecta hacia abajo → momentos invertidos.</p>
#hide
'Extraer fuerzas de los 5 segmentos de la viga Sur (nodos 5-6, 6-7, 7-8, 8-9, 9-10)
P_viga = vector(n_m)
V_viga = vector(n_m)
M_viga_I = vector(n_m)
M_viga_J = vector(n_m)
T_viga = vector(n_m)
x_viga_I = vector(n_m)
x_viga_J = vector(n_m)
#for ii = 0 : n_m - 1
	nI_b = n_base + ii + 1
	nJ_b = nI_b + 1
	u_b = vector(12)
	#for dd = 1 : 6
		u_b.dd = Z.((nI_b - 1)*6 + dd)
		u_b.(6 + dd) = Z.((nJ_b - 1)*6 + dd)
	#loop
	f_b = K_vxg*u_b
	seg = ii + 1
	P_viga.seg = f_b.1/g
	V_viga.seg = f_b.3/g
	M_viga_I.seg = f_b.5/g
	M_viga_J.seg = -f_b.11/g
	T_viga.seg = f_b.4/g
	x_viga_I.seg = ii*d_x
	x_viga_J.seg = (ii + 1)*d_x
#loop
'Vectores para $Plot (2 puntos por segmento: I y J)
n_pts = 2*n_m
x_plot = vector(n_pts)
M_plot = vector(n_pts)
V_plot = vector(n_pts)
T_plot = vector(n_pts)
P_plot = vector(n_pts)
#for ii = 1 : n_m
	x_plot.(2*ii - 1) = x_viga_I.ii
	x_plot.(2*ii) = x_viga_J.ii
	M_plot.(2*ii - 1) = M_viga_I.ii
	M_plot.(2*ii) = M_viga_J.ii
	V_plot.(2*ii - 1) = -V_viga.ii
	V_plot.(2*ii) = V_viga.ii
	T_plot.(2*ii - 1) = T_viga.ii
	T_plot.(2*ii) = T_viga.ii
	P_plot.(2*ii - 1) = P_viga.ii
	P_plot.(2*ii) = P_viga.ii
#loop
#show
'<h4>8.1 Momento flector M (tonf.m) — viga Sur</h4>
'<p>Convencion: negativo = viga flecta hacia abajo (traccion fibra inferior)</p>
#hide
M_v = matrix(1; n_m + 1)
V_v = matrix(1; n_m + 1)
T_v = matrix(1; n_m + 1)
P_v = matrix(1; n_m + 1)
#for ii = 1 : n_m
	M_v.(1; ii) = M_v.(1; ii) + M_viga_I.ii
	M_v.(1; ii + 1) = M_v.(1; ii + 1) + M_viga_J.ii
	V_v.(1; ii) = V_v.(1; ii) + V_viga.ii
	V_v.(1; ii + 1) = V_v.(1; ii + 1) - V_viga.ii
	T_v.(1; ii) = T_v.(1; ii) + T_viga.ii
	T_v.(1; ii + 1) = T_v.(1; ii + 1) + T_viga.ii
	P_v.(1; ii) = P_v.(1; ii) + P_viga.ii
	P_v.(1; ii + 1) = P_v.(1; ii + 1) + P_viga.ii
#loop
#for ii = 2 : n_m
	M_v.(1; ii) = M_v.(1; ii)/2
	T_v.(1; ii) = T_v.(1; ii)/2
	P_v.(1; ii) = P_v.(1; ii)/2
#loop
M_sp(x) = spline(1 + x/d_x; M_v)
V_sp(x) = spline(1 + x/d_x; V_v)
T_sp(x) = spline(1 + x/d_x; T_v)
P_sp(x) = spline(1 + x/d_x; P_v)
#show
$Plot{M_sp(x) @ x = 0 : a}
'<h4>8.2 Cortante V (tonf) — viga Sur</h4>
$Plot{V_sp(x) @ x = 0 : a}
'<h4>8.3 Torsion T (tonf.m) — viga Sur</h4>
$Plot{T_sp(x) @ x = 0 : a}
'<h4>8.4 Axial P (tonf) — viga Sur</h4>
$Plot{P_sp(x) @ x = 0 : a}
'<h4>8.5 Tabla viga Sur (5 segmentos)</h4>
#val
'<table border="1" cellpadding="4" style="border-collapse:collapse; font-size:0.9em">
'<tr style="background:#333;color:white"><th>Seg</th><th>x (m)</th><th>P (tonf)</th><th>V (tonf)</th><th>T (tonf.m)</th><th>M_I (tonf.m)</th><th>M_J (tonf.m)</th></tr>
#hide
#for ii = 1 : n_m
	#show
	#val
	'<tr><td>'ii'</td><td>'x_viga_I.ii'-'x_viga_J.ii'</td><td>'P_viga.ii'</td><td>'V_viga.ii'</td><td>'T_viga.ii'</td><td>'M_viga_I.ii'</td><td>'M_viga_J.ii'</td></tr>
	#hide
#loop
#show
'</table>
#equ
'<hr/>
'<h3>PARTE IX — Diagrama columna 1</h3>
'<p>Columna pinned base → M_base = 0, M_top = V*H</p>
#hide
P_col_val = abs(f_col_local.1)/g
V_col_val = abs(f_col_local.2)/g
M_col_top = abs(f_col_local.11)/g
M_col_base = abs(f_col_local.5)/g
T_col_val = abs(f_col_local.4)/g
x_col = [0; H_p]
M_col_plot(z) = M_col_base + (M_col_top - M_col_base)*z/H_p
V_col_plot(z) = V_col_val
P_col_plot(z) = P_col_val
#show
'<h4>9.1 Momento M2 columna (tonf.m) vs altura z</h4>
$Plot{M_col_plot(z) @ z = 0 : H_p}
'<h4>9.2 Cortante V columna (tonf)</h4>
$Plot{V_col_plot(z) @ z = 0 : H_p}
'<h4>9.3 Resumen columna 1</h4>
#val
'<table border="1" cellpadding="6" style="border-collapse:collapse;">
'<tr style="background:#333;color:white"><th>Fuerza</th><th>Base (z=0)</th><th>Top (z='H_p')</th></tr>
'<tr><td>P axial (tonf)</td><td>'P_col_val'</td><td>'P_col_val'</td></tr>
'<tr><td>V shear (tonf)</td><td>'V_col_val'</td><td>'V_col_val'</td></tr>
'<tr><td>M2 (tonf.m)</td><td>'M_col_base'</td><td>'M_col_top'</td></tr>
'<tr><td>M2 cara (tonf.m)</td><td>—</td><td>'M_face'</td></tr>
'<tr><td>T torsion (tonf.m)</td><td>'T_col_val'</td><td>'T_col_val'</td></tr>
'</table>
#equ
